## Map coloring with numbers, generated from the Rosie teaching script (english-input.txt) under the world conventions.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##   1. The name of the puzzle is number-map-color.
##   4. The name of the action is write-1-to-4.
##   5. You can write a number that is between one and four onto an empty location.
##   6. If the value of a location is absent then the location is empty.
##   8. If the value of a location is the value of an object that is next to the location then you lose.
##  10. The solution has three steps.
##  12. The name of the goal is all-filled.
##  14. The goal is that all locations are filled.
##  15. If the value of a location is more than zero then the location is filled.
## World: init-map-ncolor3rc.world (a 3x3 grid of locations, six filled; near relation between neighbors)
##
## Translation (tools/rosie-language.md gives the general reading; the assumption ledger is in README.md):
##   - "an object that is next to the location": the near relation of the world file (A-L2).
##   - Operator write (argument1 = the location, argument2 = number-k for k from 1 to 4).

## Propose initialize-number-map-color when its conditions below hold.
sp {number-map-color*propose*initialize-number-map-color
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-number-map-color ^task-operator false)
}

sp {number-map-color*apply*initialize-number-map-color
   (state <s> ^operator.name initialize-number-map-color ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^objects <objs>)
-->
   (<s> ^name number-map-color ^desireds <ds>)
   (<objs> ^object <o-loc-1-1> <o-loc-1-2> <o-loc-1-3> <o-loc-2-1> <o-loc-2-2> <o-loc-2-3> <o-loc-3-1> <o-loc-3-2> <o-loc-3-3> <o-task> <o-number-1> <o-number-2> <o-number-3> <o-number-4>)
   (<o-loc-1-1> ^object-handle loc-1-1 ^anchored true ^type location ^row 1 ^column 1)
   (<o-loc-1-2> ^object-handle loc-1-2 ^anchored true ^type location ^value 2 ^row 1 ^column 2)
   (<o-loc-1-3> ^object-handle loc-1-3 ^anchored true ^type location ^value 4 ^row 1 ^column 3)
   (<o-loc-2-1> ^object-handle loc-2-1 ^anchored true ^type location ^value 3 ^row 2 ^column 1)
   (<o-loc-2-2> ^object-handle loc-2-2 ^anchored true ^type location ^value 1 ^row 2 ^column 2)
   (<o-loc-2-3> ^object-handle loc-2-3 ^anchored true ^type location ^value 3 ^row 2 ^column 3)
   (<o-loc-3-1> ^object-handle loc-3-1 ^anchored true ^type location ^value 4 ^row 3 ^column 1)
   (<o-loc-3-2> ^object-handle loc-3-2 ^anchored true ^type location ^row 3 ^column 2)
   (<o-loc-3-3> ^object-handle loc-3-3 ^anchored true ^type location ^row 3 ^column 3)
   (<o-task> ^object-handle task ^anchored true ^type task)
   (<o-number-1> ^object-handle number-1 ^anchored true ^type number ^number 1)
   (<o-number-2> ^object-handle number-2 ^anchored true ^type number ^number 2)
   (<o-number-3> ^object-handle number-3 ^anchored true ^type number ^number 3)
   (<o-number-4> ^object-handle number-4 ^anchored true ^type number ^number 4)
   (<ds> ^desired-count 1 ^desired <d1>)
   (<d1> ^object <d1-o>)
   (<d1-o> ^object-handle task ^goal-met true)
   (<w> ^empty <empty-loc-1-1>)
   (<empty-loc-1-1> ^argument1 <o-loc-1-1>)
   (<w> ^empty <empty-loc-3-2>)
   (<empty-loc-3-2> ^argument1 <o-loc-3-2>)
   (<w> ^empty <empty-loc-3-3>)
   (<empty-loc-3-3> ^argument1 <o-loc-3-3>)
